{
    "title": "phpolars and plain PHP arrays",
    "description": "Plain PHP arrays are the baseline that a PHP data frame library starts from. The data are a 1M-row CSV (k: 100,000 keys, g: 50 groups, x: integers with 2% missing, y: floats; 22 MB) and a 100,000-row lookup table on k. Each case runs once to warm up and then five times; the value is the median. The plain PHP code reads rows with fgetcsv, groups with one loop over an associative array, and joins with a hash index of the lookup table. phpolars uses 2 Polars threads. Results stay in Polars; converting them to PHP arrays is not timed.",
    "measure": "Wall time",
    "unit": "ms",
